{
  "name": "pufferfish",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/pufferfish.py): a pufferfish (a porcupine-puffer, blown up), 25 cm -- a ROUND body puffed like a ball, bristling with SPINES standing out all over it (rings of `horn`s leaning back, a few down the back's ridge); a small BEAK of fused teeth, pale plates above and below a slot, at the front; big green eyes high on the head; no belly fins -- small pectorals, the dorsal and anal set far back over the tail's stalk, a little rounded tail; yellow-brown above with DARK SPOTS (the coat pattern `trout`, its red spots kept off), a white belly. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A slow SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing).",
